# story0015_check_output_format.txtar — STORY-0015 / TASK-0036:
# --check + --output-format interaction.
#
# runCheck compares "before" (re-encoded in input format) vs "after" (encoded
# in output format). When the two formats differ, the serialisations are never
# byte-identical — even an identity query always produces drift.
#
# 1. Same format (json→json): identity query → no drift → exit 0.
nesdit input.json --check --output-format json --query '.'
! stdout .
! stderr .

# 2. Cross format (json→yaml): identity query → always drifts → exit 2.
! nesdit input.json --check --output-format yaml --query '.'
! stdout .

-- input.json --
{"x":1}
